# Sino-US Green Finance Cooperation (2016–2022)—An Empirical Analysis Based on Texts

**Authors:** Wenjing Wang, Taiyi He, Jingcheng Lin, Haoxiang Zhao, Zezheng Qin, Kunhao Dai

## Abstract
Green finance cooperation is an organic component of international cooperation among the globalization, but few studies focused on the status of green finance cooperation. Previous studies have confirmed the value of green finance cooperation within countries for green development, laying the foundation for initiating discussions on green finance cooperation between countries. This paper uses quantitative methods such as word frequency statistical analysis, visualization cloud map, and semantic network analysis to analyze the development process of Sino-US green finance cooperation on the basis of selected green finance cooperation texts. The results show that multi-dimensional parties in Sino-US green finance cooperation play a role in promoting the cooperation process and resolving differences in cooperation cognition. Secondly, the auxiliary elements of Sino-US green finance cooperation have achieved value mobilization and effective integration. Thirdly, the development effect of Sino-US green finance cooperation has a relatively sensitive response to external shocks represented by political factors.

